          "title": "Signals in Angular w/ Pawel and Alex",
          "duration": "5:23:37",
          "channel": "Ryan Carniato",
          "description": "Signals seem to be taking the web dev world by storm. But the truth is much longer in the making. Friday's stream I hang out with Angular core team members Pawel and Alex to talk about their journey into Fine-Grained Reactivity.\n\nSignals in Angular w/ Pawel Kozlowski and Alex Rickabaugh\n\n[0:00] Preamble\n[7:30] Welcome Pawel Kozlowski and Alex Rickabaugh\n[14:00] The context surrounding Angular's emergence\n[21:30] Introduction to \"Zones\" in Angular\n[25:30] Excalidraw! The three types of rendering\n[36:00] How does RxJS fit into this?\n[41:00] onPush Vs. zone.js\n[47:00] How Pawel learned about signals\n[50:30] How signals fit into Angular\n[56:30] The three reactive language primitives\n[59:30] Reactivity in RxJS - Streams and Behavior Subjects\n[1:10:00] Observables - Hot/Cold and Unicast/Multicast\n[1:15:00] How RxJS and Signals work better together than zone.js/RxJS\n[1:24:30] How the Angular team landed on signals\n[1:27:30] Segregating read/write activity the right way\n[1:37:45] Code - example of Angular's signals\n[1:42:00] Code - The getter primitive\n[1:48:30] Code - effect and computed\n[1:51:30] Code - Putting this into context\n[1:56:15] Excalidraw! Simple diamond problem w/ Angular signals\n[2:04:15] More complex examples\n[2:10:00] How it works\n[2:18:15] How Angular signals compare to other solutions\n[2:24:45] The gang waxes poetic about signals\n[2:35:15] Q & A: What was Angular's history with two-way data binding?\n[2:36:15] Q & A: Are there plans for nested reactivity?\n[2:39:00] Q & A: What about Svelte stores in Angular?\n[2:42:00] Q & A: Can I nest effects?\n[2:50:30] Garbage collection with lazy reactivity\n[3:03:45] What's next for Angular Signals?\n[3:10:00] Using the Angular compiler\n[3:15:45] Trends in the JS community\n[3:22:00] Q & A: What will the roll-out for signals in Angular look like?\n[3:27:00] Q & A: Other headline features?\n[3:28:00] Q & A: How will circular dependencies be handled?\n[3:31:30] Q & A: JSX in Angular when!?!?\n[3:33:30] Q & A: Will we have full support of JS syntax in component metadata?\n[3:35:45] Q & A: How do signals fit into the SSR story?\n[3:37:30] Farewell to Alex and Pawel\n\nThis Week in JavaScript\n\n[3:41:30] Introduction\n[3:42:30] Syntax Podcast\n[3:43:00] Explaining the partnership with Astro and Tanner Linsley.\n[3:46:30] Yet Another Launcher\n[3:47:00] Dan Jutan is back! (tutorial videos)\n[3:47:45] Sarah Drasner's Angular Signals video\n[3:48:55] JavaScript Jabber podcast\n[3:49:15] Dominic Gannaway's new framework\n[3:53:00] Qwik's server functions\n[3:56:00] Milo's reactivity graphs\n[3:57:15] JavaScript Twitter drama... but WAIT!\n[3:58:30] MarkoJS TypeScript support!!\n[4:02:45] Back to the Twitter drama\n[4:06:00] Svelte streaming\n[4:09:30] The deleted tweet and Remix backlash\n[4:12:15] Ryan's response\n[4:21:45] Ryan Florence deactivated his Twitter.\n[4:32:00] Andrew Clark's tweets\n[4:47:00] Showing some differences in code\n[5:06:30] The drawbacks of working with signals \n[5:16:15] Wrapping up\n\nThanks @zombiefacesupreme for the timestamps",
